<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:48:23Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>How big is Russia's threat against Germany?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b45ad8b9c15cd91f73fb8c49c28f3f846096118dd52be8b024dccec7b4dae1d</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-big-is-russia-s-threat-against-germany/a-79688426--e8db9669a70a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-big-is-russia-s-threat-against-germany/a-79688426?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Experts believe that, so far, Germany has been ill-prepared — both militarily and mentally — for Russian provocations. They also warn against the idea that ending support for Ukraine would make Germany safer.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Berlin's leftist parties move step closer to forming government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7af483561d79e22bbf87e5fa4a7a57cdfcb607b245e08138c446a99397ea73d</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:48:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T10:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-s-leftist-parties-move-step-closer-to-forming-government/live-79686913--8bbbc4d4b09d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-s-leftist-parties-move-step-closer-to-forming-government/live-79686913?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin's left-leaning parties have successfully concluded exploratory talks, and formal coalition negotiations could begin next month if party members approve. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, France agree on deal to support Europe's struggling car industry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:284fa29cf92820bcfc86bba73de016ae35f7113c8d3851541b91ef57c0599efb</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-france-agree-on-deal-to-support-europe-s-struggling-car-industry/a-79678595--5e23597ac466.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-france-agree-on-deal-to-support-europe-s-struggling-car-industry/a-79678595?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The two countries said the agreement aimed to safeguard Europe's automotive industry, encouraging development and research. Automakers in Europe have so far struggled to compete with Chinese electric car companies.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German lawmakers back monthly state pension contributions for children, with families able to add more.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ada53c0b3571a2360a16c8c0ee9d4bda146fbc268833b6ab85c848bf8ce228b2</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T11:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-lawmakers-back-monthly-state-pension-contributions-for-children-with-families-able-to-add-mor/live-79678671--02713419dab3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-lawmakers-back-monthly-state-pension-contributions-for-children-with-families-able-to-add-more/live-79678671?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's parliament has backed a plan to help children save for retirement from the age of 6. Meanwhile, Jewish students report death threats after they confronted a far-right lawmaker.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Isha Bhatia Sanan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c66e8e49bdaf78c47483e208fe4a349f2193078200e7b92b9e22fd06c1652b5</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/isha-bhatia-sanan/a-79678415--251eb4c8b016.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/isha-bhatia-sanan/a-79678415?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Isha Bhatia Sanan is DW’s Bureau Chief in India, leading the broadcaster’s operations in Delhi and Chennai.</summary><category term="Our Experts" /></entry><entry><title>Who was Eva Mamlok? Berlin square renamed after Jewish anti-fascist resistance fighter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f77daadec4f408f1389e7dc5ec4afdb2dba33f256dc96cc4a3402125656dc852</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919--fa371a8e7f27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She started taking action against Hitler as a teenager and never stopped until her death in a concentration camp. Berlin's Blücherplatz is now being renamed after her.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Resignation of Bärbel Bas shines light on harsh era of German politics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6f888e66d991584636e855832edceea23e28b31d53d6d5413575c04f8ccd9ee</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/resignation-of-b_rbel-bas-shines-light-on-harsh-era-of-german-politics/a-79671395--56c0e1283306.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/resignation-of-bärbel-bas-shines-light-on-harsh-era-of-german-politics/a-79671395?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Labor Minister Bärbel Bas has stepped down, citing her need to grieve a loved one and leave behind the harsh realities of government. So how did German politics get so heated?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands of German gamblers could sue for their money back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47bf3753f99056973b4f8cee670b5879ed3e3eb8f244beaa28cac641c92d7d90</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T10:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/thousands-of-german-gamblers-could-sue-for-their-money-back/a-79667844--bc7691d0e6e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/thousands-of-german-gamblers-could-sue-for-their-money-back/a-79667844?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German gamblers may finally be able to beat the house, thanks to new court rulings in the EU and in Germany. The decisions could help gambling addicts — but the legal road might be difficult.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>'Ragebait' is the 2026 German Youth Word of the Year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:224f082c59f6fe29f2c649ce513f9dada024dbce3912240b212e6fcb1bca78ac</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158--c39c4c350c71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Already named the 2025 Oxford Word of the Year, "rage bait" has also been widely adopted in German slang.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Author or artificial intelligence? Literature in crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2982cfff49673da22c8690a6a13a8e5e149cbe8c5135dcf1fab0e65936f303c</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610--2ddbca94bc5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI is a hot topic at this year's Frankfurt Book Fair. An international literary scandal has raised questions about machine-generated texts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eb74ecf285f2b33fdc418ead1d33e89c82615450c63b0536f03f141569f9248</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism, and are taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
